          "margin": "0"
        },
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Five hours after launch, with the Sun behind them, the last crew to go to the Moon saw the Earth fully lit. Africa, Arabia and the Antarctic ice cap sit in one frame, 29,000 kilometres out. It became one of the most reproduced photographs ever made."
      },
