          "font-size": "1.0625rem",
          "line-height": "1.55",
          "margin": "0"
        },
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Six billion kilometres from the Sun, its main mission over, Voyager 1 turned its camera around one last time. The Earth takes up a fraction of a single pixel, caught in a band of sunlight scattered inside the instrument. Thirty-four minutes later the cameras were switched off for good."
      },
