        "c1-body": {
          "attrs": {},
          "breakpoints": {
            "mobile": {
              "font-size": "0.9375rem",
              "line-height": "1.45"
            }
          },
          "children": [],
          "id": "c1-body",
          "name": "C1 body",
          "styles": {
            "color": "var(--night-soft)",
            "font-size": "1.0625rem",
            "line-height": "1.55",
            "margin": "0"
          },
          "tag": "p",
          "text": "On the fourth orbit of the Moon the spacecraft rolled, and the Earth came up over the horizon. William Anders asked for a colour magazine and took the picture that was not on the flight plan. Home was about 380,000 kilometres away."
        },
